  "hostChanges": [
    "Reentrant storage lock and SingleThreadValue owner use one immutable Worker owner; no JVM contention or interrupts provided.",
    "Default maps retain null-key rejection and real map get/put/remove operations; provided maps remain caller-owned.",
    "Cancellation classification uses an explicit ProcessCanceledException class/subclass marker, replacing reflection over JVM class names; no IntelliJ service implementation is supplied.",
    "Storage map API source declarations preserve bodies and only alias ConcurrentMap to MutableMap for a serial host.",
    "Kotlin nullable/non-null Function0/Function1 adapters share the original state machines instead of Java flexible generic inheritance.",
    "Diagnostic object IDs and JVM stack-trace sanitization are host-specific; error type, propagation, cache and recursion behavior are retained.",
    "closeQuietly uses a real common closeable interface with original catch-and-ignore behavior."
  ],
